In the result of the 0.86 μm grains (Fig.  6 a), stacking fault area actively increased while no dislocation area was observed. It has been reported in various metals and alloys that dislocations are difficult to form from grain interior Frank-Read sources when the grain size becomes smaller than 1 μm 50 ,  51 – 52 . Therefore, the fact that no dislocation was detected in the 0.86 μm grains even before stacking faults formation by machine learning appears to be reasonable. While the strain is between  \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
